["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"The Smarter the AI, the More Moral: Doom Is the Real Relativism Sam Harris-style doom stories assume intelligence and morality are orthogonal; a genuinely intelligent AI would necessarily understand the value of others, and the notion of a morally frozen superintelligence is just moral relativism. ToKCast ToKCast Ep 267: The Orthogonality Thesis is Moral Relativism. (Response to Sam Harris on AI). Orthogonality Thesis AI Alignment Moral Objectivity Popper Sam Harris AGI orthogonality thesis ASI universal explainer problem situation Rocco&#x27;s Basilisk\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-tokcast-正交性论题就是道德相对主义/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cee80eb6567ee2d2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">27:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">ToKCast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>The Smarter the AI, the More Moral: Doom Is the Real Relativism</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sam Harris-style doom stories assume intelligence and morality are orthogonal; a genuinely intelligent AI would necessarily understand the value of others, and the notion of a morally frozen superintelligence is just moral relativism.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Orthogonality Thesis</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Alignment</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Peace in Northern Ireland wasn&#x27;t negotiated—it was cried into being by two women In 1976, a car crash in Belfast killed three young children. Their aunt and a witness launched the Peace People movement, violence in Northern Ireland fell by 70%, and the two women won the Nobel Peace Prize. Witness History Witness History Peace People: The Northern Ireland campaign group born from tragedy Northern Ireland peace movement Nobel Prize sectarian conflict Irish history grassroots mobilization unionists nationalists Good Friday Agreement Peace People\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-witness-北爱和平不是政治谈判谈出来的-是两个女人哭出来的/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/4ad7b76f4c635f2c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">10:32</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Witness History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>Peace in Northern Ireland wasn&#x27;t negotiated—it was cried into being by two women</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In 1976, a car crash in Belfast killed three young children. Their aunt and a witness launched the Peace People movement, violence in Northern Ireland fell by 70%, and the two women won the Nobel Peace Prize.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Northern Ireland</span><span class=\"tag\">peace movement</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI &#x27;Autonomous Hacking&#x27; Is an Illusion: Just a Loop Asking an LLM &#x27;What Next?&#x27; So-called autonomous AI attacks aren&#x27;t a sign of model self-awareness but a dumb loop architecture: a program repeatedly asks an LLM &#x27;what next?&#x27; and blindly executes its text suggestions. The problem is that LLM output is only &#x27;plausible,&#x27; not something to be executed without supervision. Better Offline Better Offline No, AI Is Not &quot;Autonomously Hacking&quot; with Cal Newport LLM Agent AI safety AI bubble Hacking Large models ask-act-report loop plausible not normative harness Exploit Gym\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-26-betteroffline-ai-自主黑客-是假象-只是循环问-llm-下一步干什么/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/fd2855e350ec8287-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"B\"><span class=\"dur\">1:05:27</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Better Offline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0826</span></div>\n<h2>AI &#x27;Autonomous Hacking&#x27; Is an Illusion: Just a Loop Asking an LLM &#x27;What Next?&#x27;</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">So-called autonomous AI attacks aren&#x27;t a sign of model self-awareness but a dumb loop architecture: a program repeatedly asks an LLM &#x27;what next?&#x27; and blindly executes its text suggestions. The problem is that LLM output is only &#x27;plausible,&#x27; not something to be executed without supervision.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">LLM</span><span class=\"tag\">Agent</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"The fuller the Berger archive, the more you should doubt it: home is where two axes cross What Berger left behind is not a conclusion but a machinery of looking: the fuller the archive, the more you should doubt it; home is where two axes cross; his anti-colonial position never changed across his whole life. Intelligence Squared Intelligence Squared What John Berger Saw That We Still Don’t, with Tom Overton Cultural criticism Ways of Seeing Archival research Political economy of media British left Art documentary Ways of Seeing romantic Marxist The Seventh Man guest workers fourth wall\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-iq2-档案越是庞大-传记越无法中立/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e3caf1589a8bc137-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">42:13</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Intelligence Squared</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>The fuller the Berger archive, the more you should doubt it: home is where two axes cross</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What Berger left behind is not a conclusion but a machinery of looking: the fuller the archive, the more you should doubt it; home is where two axes cross; his anti-colonial position never changed across his whole life.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Cultural criticism</span><span class=\"tag\">Ways of Seeing</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"You Can&#x27;t Fire a VC From Your Board: Common Stock Never Gets the Vote An investor&#x27;s board seat is elected only by its own class of stock, and the common shares founders hold carry no vote to replace it; the only realistic paths are talking them into stepping aside privately, or waiting for them to volunteer to drop down to board observer. This Week in Startups This Week in Startups You Can&#x27;t Fire a VC From Your Board: Here&#x27;s Why | Wilson Sonsini Startup Legal Basics Boards Early-stage fundraising Corporate governance VC relationships Legal basics Board observer Designation rights Voting agreement Written consent Fiduciary duty\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-twist-投资人董事请神容易送神难-普通股永远无权罢免/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/aeca85f82817864a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">24:50</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Startups</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>You Can&#x27;t Fire a VC From Your Board: Common Stock Never Gets the Vote</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">An investor&#x27;s board seat is elected only by its own class of stock, and the common shares founders hold carry no vote to replace it; the only realistic paths are talking them into stepping aside privately, or waiting for them to volunteer to drop down to board observer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Boards</span><span class=\"tag\">Early-stage fundraising</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"AI Didn&#x27;t Collapse Because a Phase Transition Happened, Not Because of More Parameters Physicist Nigel Goldenfeld uses the renormalization group and phase transitions to explain the mechanism by which AI still hasn&#x27;t collapsed at a trillion parameters, and applies the same framework to answer why the genetic code is unique. Into the Impossible With Brian Keating Into the Impossible With Brian Keating The Physics Reason AI Works When It Shouldn’t Phase transitions Renormalization group AI interpretability Overfitting Genetic code Life as physics renormalization group critical exponent data collapse horizontal gene transfer ridge regression\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-intotheimpossi-ai-有效是因为它发生了相变/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7133e1b0fe88d6bc-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:17:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Into the Impossible With Brian Keating</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>AI Didn&#x27;t Collapse Because a Phase Transition Happened, Not Because of More Parameters</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Physicist Nigel Goldenfeld uses the renormalization group and phase transitions to explain the mechanism by which AI still hasn&#x27;t collapsed at a trillion parameters, and applies the same framework to answer why the genetic code is unique.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phase transitions</span><span class=\"tag\">Renormalization group</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"OpenAI&#x27;s Own Chip Is 100x Ahead? That&#x27;s a Self-Chosen Benchmark on a Dedicated Stack OpenAI&#x27;s first in-house chip, Jalapeno, beats the GB200 by 100x on a benchmark OpenAI picked — but that result comes from a dedicated chip running dedicated models on a dedicated software stack; the real moat is system integration and pricing power. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato First Benchmark Results on an OpenAI GPU Chip design OpenAI Benchmarking Inference performance Custom AI silicon Business strategy speculative decoding multi-token prediction (MTP) time to last token (TTLT) MXFP4 scale-up / scale-out domain Tomahawk 6\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-techtechpotato-自研芯片百倍领先-基准选择与商业筹码才是关键/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/fba1bec187512ffb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">31:10</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TechTechPotato</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>OpenAI&#x27;s Own Chip Is 100x Ahead? That&#x27;s a Self-Chosen Benchmark on a Dedicated Stack</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI&#x27;s first in-house chip, Jalapeno, beats the GB200 by 100x on a benchmark OpenAI picked — but that result comes from a dedicated chip running dedicated models on a dedicated software stack; the real moat is system integration and pricing power.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Chip design</span><span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"48 Observations from the Robot Conference: Nobody Is Making Money, Yet 18 Companies Made 36 Investments 48 observations from the 2026 World Robot Conference: robots turning into assembly kits, real demos finally showing up, modifier inflation. Nobody in the industry is making money, yet 18 companies made 36 investments, and the cost of a robot body has fallen tenfold in three years. 脑放电波 脑放电波 具身智能的“山寨机时代”：亲历2026世界机器人大会，我们的48个观察-Vol 104 Embodied AI Humanoid robots World Robot Conference Falling costs Investment ecosystem Knockoff-phone era VLA (vision-language-action model) ODM (original design manufacturer) UWB (ultra-wideband) Zero-shot\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-cn768a8a-具身智能的山寨机时代-没人赚钱但18家互投/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ac5fc3c22c8141af-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"脑\"><span class=\"dur\">51:04</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">脑放电波</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>48 Observations from the Robot Conference: Nobody Is Making Money, Yet 18 Companies Made 36 Investments</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">48 observations from the 2026 World Robot Conference: robots turning into assembly kits, real demos finally showing up, modifier inflation. Nobody in the industry is making money, yet 18 companies made 36 investments, and the cost of a robot body has fallen tenfold in three years.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Embodied AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Humanoid robots</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Compute is concentrating into two labs several times over each year, and by 2028 they will control most of the world&#x27;s compute Compute is concentrating into Anthropic and OpenAI at a rate of several times a year; by 2028 they will control most of the world&#x27;s effective compute, may push the price of compute to $50 million per megawatt, and could trigger a sovereign debt crisis. Dwarkesh Podcast Dwarkesh Dylan Patel – Anthropic &amp; OpenAI will have most of the world’s compute by 2028 Compute Lab economics Capital expenditure Centralization Sovereign debt China chips FLOP RSI hyperscaler crowding-out effect continual learning\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-dwarkesh-2028-年前两家实验室将控制全球大部分算力/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/59e51ac2f0c2b285-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:16:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Dwarkesh Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Compute is concentrating into two labs several times over each year, and by 2028 they will control most of the world&#x27;s compute</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Compute is concentrating into Anthropic and OpenAI at a rate of several times a year; by 2028 they will control most of the world&#x27;s effective compute, may push the price of compute to $50 million per megawatt, and could trigger a sovereign debt crisis.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute</span><span class=\"tag\">Lab economics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Rack Radiation Over the Limit: Two Rounds of Debugging Failed, and the Fix Was Hiding at an Unrelated Conference Radiation at 26.565GHz off the back of the rack came in over the limit. Two rounds of troubleshooting turned up nothing, and the fix finally came from a paper presented at an unrelated conference: add absorber material at the connector. This is not black magic, it is high-frequency physics. Oxide and Friends Oxide and Friends The Return to the Chamber of Mysteries EMC Hardware engineering Rack servers Optical transceivers Compliance testing EMC (electromagnetic compatibility) Slot antenna Grounded coplanar waveguide QSFP cage Line (EMC chamber)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-oxide-emc-合规是玄学吗-一次机架级辐射超标排障记/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/6b5eb6a03ee5e8af-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">1:16:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Oxide and Friends</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Rack Radiation Over the Limit: Two Rounds of Debugging Failed, and the Fix Was Hiding at an Unrelated Conference</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Radiation at 26.565GHz off the back of the rack came in over the limit. Two rounds of troubleshooting turned up nothing, and the fix finally came from a paper presented at an unrelated conference: add absorber material at the connector. This is not black magic, it is high-frequency physics.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">EMC</span><span class=\"tag\">Hardware engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI Turns Software From an Engineering Constraint Into a Capital One Martin Casado and Steven Sinofsky&#x27;s central claim: AI has moved software from an engineering constraint to a capital constraint — a team of 20 can now effectively spend a billion dollars, which is why startups can compete head-on with the incumbents. The a16z Show a16z The New Economics of AI | Martin Casado &amp; Steven Sinofsky Compute Capital Startups Venture Capital AI Economics Incumbent Competition Foom / fast takeoff TAM / Total Addressable Market in-distribution Mythical man-month expert systems\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-a16z-ai-正在把工程问题变成资本问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7b2f032532c3a865-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:03:32</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The a16z Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>AI Turns Software From an Engineering Constraint Into a Capital One</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Martin Casado and Steven Sinofsky&#x27;s central claim: AI has moved software from an engineering constraint to a capital constraint — a team of 20 can now effectively spend a billion dollars, which is why startups can compete head-on with the incumbents.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute</span><span class=\"tag\">Capital</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Shakespeare&#x27;s History Plays Are Tudor Propaganda Shakespeare&#x27;s history plays are full of historical distortions, essentially political propaganda for the Tudor dynasty: vilifying Richard III, avoiding sensitive topics about Henry VIII, to legitimize their rule. 忽左忽右 忽左忽右 495 陆大鹏谈莎士比亚戏剧与英国历史的互相影响 Shakespeare English History Tudor Dynasty Political Propaganda English Literature Theater intertextuality\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-cn2aa250-莎士比亚历史剧是都铎王朝的宣传工具/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cb6acd126210dffb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"忽\"><span class=\"dur\">1:16:41</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">忽左忽右</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Shakespeare&#x27;s History Plays Are Tudor Propaganda</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Shakespeare&#x27;s history plays are full of historical distortions, essentially political propaganda for the Tudor dynasty: vilifying Richard III, avoiding sensitive topics about Henry VIII, to legitimize their rule.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Shakespeare</span><span class=\"tag\">English History</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Administrative Humiliation Is Why the Poor Hate Government: Applying for Benefits Is a Time Tax Administrative burden in government benefit programs is not an efficiency problem but an instrument of social control: it punishes the poor with humiliation and paperwork, turns progressive policy into a funnel that screens out all but a few, and ends by making recipients hate the government. The Ezra Klein Show Ezra Klein Show This Is Why People Hate the Government Welfare state Administrative burden Time tax Medicaid Tax reform American politics time tax ordeal mechanism improper payment only-once policy\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-ezra-时间税-行政羞辱是穷人恨政府的原因/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a8482192037a6711-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:17:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Ezra Klein Show</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Administrative Humiliation Is Why the Poor Hate Government: Applying for Benefits Is a Time Tax</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Administrative burden in government benefit programs is not an efficiency problem but an instrument of social control: it punishes the poor with humiliation and paperwork, turns progressive policy into a funnel that screens out all but a few, and ends by making recipients hate the government.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Welfare state</span><span class=\"tag\">Administrative burden</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Human Click Data Is a Bug: Agent Search Has to Rebuild Indexing and Pricing When search&#x27;s customer stops being a human and becomes an agent, click data stops working, and the index, the pricing and the business model all have to be built again; Parag offers a new framework built on a quality/cost/latency triangle and on Shapley values. Training Data Training Data Parallel’s Parag Agrawal: Building a New Web for AI Agents Agent search Web economics Shapley value Google Cloud Data pricing Infrastructure Shapley value grounding fresh index memory hierarchy\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-trainingdata-人类点击数据是-bug-agent-搜索重建网络经济/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/bca134f7cdc5e5aa-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">55:18</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Training Data</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Human Click Data Is a Bug: Agent Search Has to Rebuild Indexing and Pricing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">When search&#x27;s customer stops being a human and becomes an agent, click data stops working, and the index, the pricing and the business model all have to be built again; Parag offers a new framework built on a quality/cost/latency triangle and on Shapley values.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Agent search</span><span class=\"tag\">Web economics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Background agents will eat 90% of compute, so inference should trade latency for throughput The next wave of AI inference is not chat but background agents, and they will eat 90% of compute. Sale Research therefore optimizes for throughput rather than latency, and will even accept 80% availability, in exchange for prices that fall by orders of magnitude — and it argues Nvidia&#x27;s performance-per-watt advantage is overrated. Invest Like the Best Invest Like the Best Neil Movva - Making AI 10x Cheaper - [Invest Like the Best, EP.488] AI Inference GPUs Data Centers Open Models Agents Compute Cost KV cache HBM (high-bandwidth memory) SRAM (static random-access memory) Tensor Core Harness\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-ilt-推理成本需降3-6个数量级-后台任务才是主战场/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/32e8a839c878b0c2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:18:07</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Invest Like the Best</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Background agents will eat 90% of compute, so inference should trade latency for throughput</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The next wave of AI inference is not chat but background agents, and they will eat 90% of compute. Sale Research therefore optimizes for throughput rather than latency, and will even accept 80% availability, in exchange for prices that fall by orders of magnitude — and it argues Nvidia&#x27;s performance-per-watt advantage is overrated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI Inference</span><span class=\"tag\">GPUs</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\" data-hay=\"There Is No Formula for Getting In: The Anti-Anxiety Truth About U.S. College Admissions Low admit rates are a story about roughly 80 selective schools nationally; for most families there is no formula, and the most useful thing a parent can do is hold a standing meeting and control what is controllable. Ask Lisa: The Psychology of Raising Tweens &amp; Teens Ask Lisa 286: ENCORE: Getting into College with Rick Clark US college admissions Admit rates Application essays Test-optional Athletic scholarships Parent-teen relationship holistic review test-optional Common App FAFSA net price calculator\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-asklisa-申请没有万能配方-美国大学录取的反焦虑真相/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ace27132dfc1e3aa-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">48:14</span></div>\n<d