; it proves the men who carried out the killing knew exactly what they were doing, and it is a reminder that understanding the Holocaust means looking at the perpetrators.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Holocaust</span><span class=\"tag\">Nazis</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Twenty Thousand Robots Shipped, Nine in Ten Idle: Embodied AI Enters Its ROI Era Beneath the heat of WRC, there may be only one or two startups genuinely doing pre-training, real deployment demand may be only 10% of shipments, and the industry has moved on from demo theater into a hands-on phase where ROI has to be calculated. 卫诗婕｜漫谈Light the Star 漫谈Light the Star 84.49 家央企采买进场，史上最热WRC：泡沫被挤压，具身行业进入实战阶段｜14 年从业者的行家鉴别指南 Embodied AI Humanoid Robots WRC World Models Data Pipeline Robotics Investment VLA / Vision-Language-Action model World Model Teleoperation EMG / Electromyography signals Data Pipeline Post-training\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-lightstar-两万台出货九成吃灰-具身行业进入算roi的实战期/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/adbddf5c93cfc63c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"卫\"><span class=\"dur\">1:02:50</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">卫诗婕｜漫谈Light the Star</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Twenty Thousand Robots Shipped, Nine in Ten Idle: Embodied AI Enters Its ROI Era</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Beneath the heat of WRC, there may be only one or two startups genuinely doing pre-training, real deployment demand may be only 10% of shipments, and the industry has moved on from demo theater into a hands-on phase where ROI has to be calculated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Embodied AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Humanoid Robots</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Intel Drops EMIB for UCIe: 1.2GB of Cache Behind 256 Cores Diamond Rapids is expected in 2027 with up to 256 P-cores, 1.2GB of last-level cache and 16 channels of DDR5; it replaces EMIB with trimmable compute building blocks and a UCIe interconnect, and the huge cache is its answer to the AI era. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato How Intel&#x27;s New CPU Finally Makes Sense CPU architecture Data centers Intel Xeon Chiplets Last-level cache AI infrastructure Fan-out fabric architecture Compute building block Fabric hub UCIe Foveros 3D Direct\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-25-techtechpotato-下一代-xeon-把宝押在-1-2gb-末级缓存上/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/fc7c90dc34e0b3f0-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">21:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TechTechPotato</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0825</span></div>\n<h2>Intel Drops EMIB for UCIe: 1.2GB of Cache Behind 256 Cores</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Diamond Rapids is expected in 2027 with up to 256 P-cores, 1.2GB of last-level cache and 16 channels of DDR5; it replaces EMIB with trimmable compute building blocks and a UCIe interconnect, and the huge cache is its answer to the AI era.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">CPU architecture</span><span class=\"tag\">Data centers</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"95% of AI Agent Projects Die in Pilot: What&#x27;s Missing Isn&#x27;t Intelligence, It&#x27;s a Control Layer AI has moved from generating content to acting on its own. 95% of agent projects are stuck in pilot and never reach production, because what&#x27;s missing isn&#x27;t intelligence but a runtime control layer. Eye On A.I. Eye On A.I. 95% of AI Agent Projects Fail to Reach Production. Here&#x27;s Why | Manoj Saxena, TrustWise Agents AI governance Enterprise software Runtime control Token cost runtime governance AI control tower guardian agents semantic action layer trust posture management\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-24-eyeonai-智能体流量首超人类-ai-失控才是落地最大瓶颈/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b277eb062496b5a5-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:01:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Eye On A.I.</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0824</span></div>\n<h2>95% of AI Agent Projects Die in Pilot: What&#x27;s Missing Isn&#x27;t Intelligence, It&#x27;s a Control Layer</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI has moved from generating content to acting on its own. 95% of agent projects are stuck in pilot and never reach production, because what&#x27;s missing isn&#x27;t intelligence but a runtime control layer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Agents</span><span class=\"tag\">AI governance</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Photonics&#x27; Third Wave: Out of the Lab in Five Years, Conquering Drones First Photons cannot interact like electrons, but wavelength multiplexing enables massive parallelism and ultra-low latency. All-optical neural networks could land within five years, with the first stop not servers but drones and real-time control. Brains and Machines Brains and Machines Will Photonics Loosen the Bottlenecks in Neural Systems? photonics neuromorphic low latency WDM SOA WDM (Wavelength Division Multiplexing) Semiconductor Optical Amplifier (SOA) McCulloch-Pitts neuron model Indium Phosphide (InP) Femtojoule per operation TDM (Time Division Multiplexing)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-24-brainsandmachi-光子计算第三次浪潮-五年内走出实验室-先征服无人机/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/9151fd6dae1293cb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"B\"><span class=\"dur\">45:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Brains and Machines</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0824</span></div>\n<h2>Photonics&#x27; Third Wave: Out of the Lab in Five Years, Conquering Drones First</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Photons cannot interact like electrons, but wavelength multiplexing enables massive parallelism and ultra-low latency. All-optical neural networks could land within five years, with the first stop not servers but drones and real-time control.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">photonics</span><span class=\"tag\">neuromorphic</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The Solid State Transformer Has Been Hyped for Fifty Years; AI Data Centers Are Its First Real Buyer The solid state transformer failed three times over — in the navy, in high-speed rail, in the smart grid — because all it offered was ‘smaller’. The copper problem and the 800-volt DC problem inside AI data centers are the first reasons it has ever had to exist. Asianometry Asianometry Has the Solid State Transformer’s Time Finally Come? Power electronics Data center power Solid state transformers 800V DC Silicon carbide Startup funding Solid State Transformer (SST) IGBT Silicon Carbide (SiC) Galvanic isolation 800VDC architecture PETT\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-24-asianometry-固态变压器吹了五十年-ai数据中心是第一个真买家/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a4d5049243d5f237-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0824</span></div>\n<h2>The Solid State Transformer Has Been Hyped for Fifty Years; AI Data Centers Are Its First Real Buyer</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The solid state transformer failed three times over — in the navy, in high-speed rail, in the smart grid — because all it offered was ‘smaller’. The copper problem and the 800-volt DC problem inside AI data centers are the first reasons it has ever had to exist.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Power electronics</span><span class=\"tag\">Data center power</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"A Pitch Tells Two Stories: The Project, And The Buyer&#x27;s Promotion Hollywood screenwriter Rhett Reese on what a pitch actually is: the project story runs on the surface, the story of the other person&#x27;s success runs underneath. Make them the protagonist, lower their risk, enlarge their reward, and your pitch lands far more often. Think Fast Talk Smart Think Fast Talk Smart 317. Plot Twist: The Second Story Hiding Inside Every Great Pitch Pitching Communication Hollywood AI Collaboration pitch gatekeeper auteur\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-24-thinkfast-好提案藏着两个故事-你的故事和对方升职的故事/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7fd7a03d438b4365-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">24:09</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Think Fast Talk Smart</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0824</span></div>\n<h2>A Pitch Tells Two Stories: The Project, And The Buyer&#x27;s Promotion</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Hollywood screenwriter Rhett Reese on what a pitch actually is: the project story runs on the surface, the story of the other person&#x27;s success runs underneath. Make them the protagonist, lower their risk, enlarge their reward, and your pitch lands far more often.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Pitching</span><span class=\"tag\">Communication</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Black Holes Have Only Two Parameters, but How They Form Is Still a Mystery Gravitational waves and the EHT confirm that black holes really do have only two parameters, but how a 120-solar-mass black hole forms, whether dark matter is made of tiny black holes, and how the last parsec gets crossed all remain unsolved. Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape Mindscape 365 | Vitor Cardoso on Why Black Holes Are Special Black holes Gravitational waves Event Horizon Telescope Dark matter Quantum gravity LISA no-hair theorem Kerr metric light ring cosmic censorship matched filtering last parsec problem\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-24-mindscape-黑洞只有两个参数-形成机制却仍是谜/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d69097efcbd03611-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:05:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0824</span></div>\n<h2>Black Holes Have Only Two Parameters, but How They Form Is Still a Mystery</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Gravitational waves and the EHT confirm that black holes really do have only two parameters, but how a 120-solar-mass black hole forms, whether dark matter is made of tiny black holes, and how the last parsec gets crossed all remain unsolved.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Black holes</span><span class=\"tag\">Gravitational waves</span>\n</div></div></a>"]